<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-15">15 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther King Jr. is born in Atlanta</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Born Michael King Jr., the son of a Baptist minister, he became the leading voice of the American civil rights movement. He received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1964 and was assassinated in 1968.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-11">11 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lateran Treaty creates Vatican City</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s government and the Holy See agreed to recognise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vatican-city">Vatican City</a> as an independent state. The treaty ended the 'Roman Question' that had divided Church and Italian state since 1870.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-14">14 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Saint Valentine's Day Massacre in Chicago</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Gunmen, some dressed as police, shot dead seven men linked to Bugs Moran's gang in a garage. The killings, widely blamed on Al Capone, turned public opinion against gangland violence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-16">16 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">First Academy Awards are presented in Hollywood</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">About 270 guests attended a dinner at the Hollywood Roosevelt Hotel where the first Oscars were handed out in around fifteen minutes. Wings won the top prize.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/slovenes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-3">3 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">King Alexander renames his realm the Kingdom of Yugoslavia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> renamed the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, 'land of the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>', as part of his royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a>. The new name was meant to override the national rivalries dividing the state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-24">24 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Black Thursday: panic selling hits Wall Street</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Nearly 13 million shares changed hands as panic swept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Stock Exchange. Bankers briefly steadied prices, but the crash that followed the next week opened the way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-29">29 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Black Tuesday: the Wall Street Crash deepens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">More than 16 million shares were sold in a day of panic on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Stock Exchange. Black Tuesday became the emblem of the crash that preceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lima-1929">Treaty of Lima (1929)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Lima, signed on 3 June 1929 with the mediation of the United States, settled the Tacna–Arica dispute left by the War of the Pacific.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/wall-street-crash-of-1929" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wall-street-crash-of-1929.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/wall-street-crash-of-1929">Wall Street crash of 1929</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Wall Street crash of 1929, also known as the Great Crash, was a stock market crash in the United States that began in October 1929 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sabilla">Battle of Sabilla</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Sabilla was fought on 29 March 1929 in Najd, central Arabia, between the forces of Ibn Saud and the Ikhwan, the tribal religious warriors who had helped him conquer Arabia but rebelled against his ban on raiding into Iraq and Kuwait and his…</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/aba-womens-war">Aba Women's War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Aba Women's War was a revolt by thousands of Igbo and Ibibio women in south-eastern Nigeria in November and December 1929.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/black-saturday-1929">Black Saturday (1929)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Black Saturday was the shooting of a peaceful Mau procession by New Zealand police in Apia, Western Samoa, on 28 December 1929.</p></div></li></ol></section>
