<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mexico"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mexico.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mexico</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Plutarco Elías Calles founds the National Revolutionary Party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Italy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Italy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Lateran Treaty creates the Vatican City State</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King Alexander imposes a dictatorship and renames the country Yugoslavia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ugarit"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Ugarit.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Ugarit</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Claude Schaeffer begins excavating Ras Shamra</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/brunei-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Brunei%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Brunei Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Oil is discovered at Seria</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-zimbabwe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Zimbabwe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Zimbabwe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gertrude Caton-Thompson’s excavations confirm the site’s African and medieval origin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/theocracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Theocracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Theocracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Lateran Treaty creates Vatican City, where the pope holds all legislative, executive and judicial power</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/natufians"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Natufians.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Natufians</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After finding similar material at el-Wad, Garrod names the Natufian culture after the Wadi Natuf</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mandatory-palestine"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mandatory%20Palestine.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mandatory Palestine</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Riots in August, including the Hebron massacre of Jews, leave 250 people dead.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/clovis-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Clovis%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Clovis culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ridgely Whiteman, aged 19, discovers the Clovis site at Blackwater Draw in eastern New Mexico</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/bauhaus"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bauhaus.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bauhaus</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The school turns its first profit under Meyer’s leadership</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/harlem-renaissance"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Harlem%20Renaissance.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Harlem Renaissance</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The stock-market crash begins the Great Depression and ends the movement’s zenith</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/negritude"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/N%C3%A9gritude.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Négritude</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jane Nardal’s article “Internationalisme noir”, on race consciousness in the African diaspora, lays a philosophical foundation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/kemalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kemalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kemalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Yakup Kadri Karaosmanoğlu uses the word Kemalism for the principles of the Turkish path to modernity</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-state-of-prussia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20State%20of%20Prussia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free State of Prussia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Blood May costs 33 lives in Berlin, and the Prussian Concordat with the Vatican is signed on 14 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/korea-under-japanese-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Korea%20under%20Japanese%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Korea under Japanese rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Gwangju Students Independence Movement of 3 November leads to the strengthening of Japanese military rule in 1931</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/jawaharlal-nehru"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jawaharlal%20Nehru.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jawaharlal Nehru</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">As Congress president at Lahore he carries the resolution for complete independence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/seville"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Seville.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Seville</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ibero-American Exposition opens</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/martin-luther-king-jr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr..png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Martin Luther King Jr.</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Born in Atlanta, Georgia, the second of three children of a Baptist minister and his wife</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/surrealism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Surrealism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Surrealism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The second Surrealist manifesto excludes members unwilling to commit to collective action, and the excluded respond with the pamphlet Un Cadavre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">New Zealand military police fire on a procession in Apia on Black Saturday, killing Tupua Tamasese Lealofi III</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/populism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Populism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Populism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Léon Lemonnier publishes a manifesto for the populist novel in France</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/trotskyism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Trotskyism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Trotskyism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Trotsky is expelled from the Soviet Union after exile to Alma-Ata in 1928</span></li></ul></section>
